      "magnitude": "Temporary positive excursion: A/E rises from about 1.01 in 2018 to 1.19 in 2021, versus a surrounding baseline near 0.95-0.97; 2018-2021 aggregate A/E is about 1.08, then reverts to about 0.96 in 2022-2024",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "evidence": [
        "artifacts/ae_tpd_by_year.csv rows 2018-2021 show AE 1.014, 1.050, 1.042, 1.186, while 2015-2017 are 0.965, 0.963, 0.957 and 2022-2024 are 0.958, 0.966, 0.949",
        "2018-2021 actual claims sum to 3419 vs expected 3170, aggregate AE about 1.08, followed by 2022-2024 actual 3022 vs expected 3156, aggregate AE about 0.96, indicating a temporary elevated sub-window",
        "Empirical A/E standard deviation for TPD is about 0.074, materially above the Poisson scale of roughly 0.035, so Poisson year-level z-scores were not used"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate TPD claims in 2018-2021, especially 2021, by diagnosis, age/gender, claim timing, coding, late claims, and any expected-basis or coding changes. Determine whether this reflects a one-off event, data issue, or temporary risk/coding shift before considering pricing or valuation adjustments."
    }
  ]
}

